1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,910
I don't believe it!

2
00:00:01,910 --> 00:00:03,120
What's wrong?

3
00:00:03,120 --> 00:00:05,320
Carter Boswell!

4
00:00:05,320 --> 00:00:06,640
Who's Carter Boswell?

5
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:08,190
He's running for the school board.

6
00:00:08,190 --> 00:00:09,590
The election's next month.

7
00:00:09,590 --> 00:00:12,000
What's wrong with wanting to be on the school board?

8
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,190
Nothing.

9
00:00:13,190 --> 00:00:16,130
But he wants to cut the school budget!

10
00:00:16,130 --> 00:00:18,580
Maybe it needs cutting.

11
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:20,530
Cutting the budget is fine,

12
00:00:20,530 --> 00:00:21,710
but he wants to do it

13
00:00:21,710 --> 00:00:23,650
by cutting all the cultural programs.

14
00:00:23,650 --> 00:00:24,920
No music, no dance,

15
00:00:24,920 --> 00:00:27,500
no concert, no stage presentations.

16
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:29,540
Why does he want to do that?

17
00:00:29,540 --> 00:00:32,230
He says it's to save the taxpayers' money,

18
00:00:32,230 --> 00:00:33,440
and I think he believes

19
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:35,110
that the taxpayers will vote for him

20
00:00:35,110 --> 00:00:38,300
if he spends less on the cultural programs.

21
00:00:38,300 --> 00:00:40,200
He's probably right.

22
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:41,730
Lots of people want their taxes

23
00:00:41,730 --> 00:00:43,400
used for new books

24
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:46,300
and a new paint job in the schoolrooms.

25
00:00:46,300 --> 00:00:48,500
Maybe some of us would like to pay a little bit more

26
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:51,620
and keep the cultural programs for our kids.

27
00:00:51,620 --> 00:00:54,360
Well, I'm not sure. Ellen.

28
00:00:54,360 --> 00:00:56,650
I hear it from my patients.

29
00:00:56,650 --> 00:01:01,920
Lots of people are tired of higher taxes.

30
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:04,080
I know,

31
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:05,190
but if Boswell wins

32
00:01:05,190 --> 00:01:07,010
he'll be an important decision-maker

33
00:01:07,010 --> 00:01:08,060
on the school board,

34
00:01:08,060 --> 00:01:09,260
and he doesn't know anything

35
00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:12,110
about our children's education.

36
00:01:12,110 --> 00:01:13,100
Who's running against him?

37
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:15,980
Nobody. That's the problem.

38
00:01:15,980 --> 00:01:18,350
Well, it sounds to me like Carter Boswell

39
00:01:18,350 --> 00:01:19,780
is going to win this seat on the board.

40
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:23,150
Oh, not if I can stop him!

41
00:01:23,150 --> 00:01:26,220
And how are you going to stop him?

42
00:01:26,220 --> 00:01:28,960
I don't know.

43
00:01:28,960 --> 00:01:31,400
Maybe I'll run against him.

44
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:37,380
Well, you've got my vote.

45
00:01:37,380 --> 00:01:39,950
I'm serious, Philip.

46
00:01:39,950 --> 00:01:42,030
Why shouldn't I run?

47
00:01:42,030 --> 00:01:44,300
Why shouldn't you run for what, Mom?

48
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:45,400
Your mother is thinking of

49
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:47,340
running for the school board.

50
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:49,420
Hey, that's terrific, Mom!

51
00:01:49,420 --> 00:01:51,120
Against Carter Boswell?

52
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:52,180
Great!

53
00:01:52,180 --> 00:01:54,050
Well, if I run for office,

54
00:01:54,050 --> 00:01:55,960
the voters will have a clear choice.

55
00:01:55,960 --> 00:01:59,240
I stand for everything Boswell doesn't.

56
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:01,690
I think a lot of people will vote for you

57
00:02:01,690 --> 00:02:03,500
against Boswell, Ellen.

58
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:05,710
I'll vote for you.

59
00:02:05,710 --> 00:02:07,650
Will you help me if I do run?

60
00:02:07,650 --> 00:02:10,300
Absolutely.

61
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:10,810
The trouble is

62
00:02:10,810 --> 00:02:14,540
it takes a little bit of money to run a campaign.

63
00:02:14,540 --> 00:02:16,770
I think you can make a difference, Ellen.

64
00:02:16,770 --> 00:02:18,190
And in a short campaign

65
00:02:18,190 --> 00:02:20,180
you wouldn't need as much money.

66
00:02:20,180 --> 00:02:21,710
You know something, Ellen?

67
00:02:21,710 --> 00:02:25,550
Why not give the people of Riverdale a clear choice?

68
00:02:25,550 --> 00:02:27,000
I'm with you.

69
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:34,870
You can make a difference.

70
00:02:34,870 --> 00:02:40,640
Come in.

71
00:02:40,640 --> 00:02:42,510
Mr. Maxwell?

72
00:02:42,510 --> 00:02:45,680
Yes, Charles Maxwell.

73
00:02:45,680 --> 00:02:48,810
My name is Ellen Stewart.

74
00:02:48,810 --> 00:02:49,390
Hello.

75
00:02:49,390 --> 00:02:55,060
Please, sit down.

76
00:02:55,060 --> 00:02:57,920
You asked to see me.

77
00:02:57,920 --> 00:03:00,270
What would you like to see me about?

78
00:03:00,270 --> 00:03:03,940
I'd like your help.

79
00:03:03,940 --> 00:03:04,860
Well,

80
00:03:04,860 --> 00:03:08,630
I'm editor of the most influential newspaper in Riverdale.

81
00:03:08,630 --> 00:03:11,470
Actually, it's the only newspaper.

82
00:03:11,470 --> 00:03:12,960
A lot of people would like my help.

83
00:03:12,960 --> 00:03:14,840
Do you have a story?

84
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:18,100
I'm planning to run for the school board.

85
00:03:18,100 --> 00:03:19,820
Against Carter Boswell?

86
00:03:19,820 --> 00:03:21,230
Yes.

87
00:03:21,230 --> 00:03:23,530
Well, that is news.

88
00:03:23,530 --> 00:03:26,230
Will you announce that I'm running?

89
00:03:26,230 --> 00:03:29,830
But I need some information.

90
00:03:29,830 --> 00:03:31,660
Of course.

91
00:03:31,660 --> 00:03:34,660
Why will the voters vote for you against Boswell,

92
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:36,950
Mrs. Stewart?

93
00:03:36,950 --> 00:03:41,020
Because I care.

94
00:03:41,020 --> 00:03:44,180
"Vote for Ellen Stewart. She cares."

95
00:03:44,180 --> 00:03:46,260
Not a bad slogan.

96
00:03:46,260 --> 00:03:49,660
But what do you care about?

97
00:03:49,660 --> 00:03:52,140
Well, I care about the children of our town.

98
00:03:52,140 --> 00:03:53,290
I don't want them to grow up

99
00:03:53,290 --> 00:03:58,000
without cultural programs in our school.

100
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,080
Do you have a plan?

101
00:04:00,080 --> 00:04:01,390
I want our children to learn

102
00:04:01,390 --> 00:04:05,780
more than reading, writing, and arithmetic.

103
00:04:05,780 --> 00:04:09,350
I want to keep the after-school programs--

104
00:04:09,350 --> 00:04:11,630
the music, the concerts.

105
00:04:11,630 --> 00:04:13,470
It's not a bad plan.

106
00:04:13,470 --> 00:04:15,360
But who's going to pay for all of this?

107
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:16,600
We are.

108
00:04:16,600 --> 00:04:18,010
The citizens of Riverdale, of course.

109
00:04:18,010 --> 00:04:23,020
I plan to get help

110
00:04:23,020 --> 00:04:25,450
That's fair enough.

111
00:04:25,450 --> 00:04:29,550
Exactly what do you want from me, Mrs. Stewart?

112
00:04:29,550 --> 00:04:30,560
You don't know me.

113
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:34,020
I can't expect you to take my side against Boswell.

114
00:04:34,020 --> 00:04:37,900
But I do need some publicity

115
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:39,030
so that the people of our town

116
00:04:39,030 --> 00:04:40,890
know that I'm running for office

117
00:04:40,890 --> 00:04:44,580
and that I care about our children.

118
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:46,300
Fair enough.

119
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:48,380
I certainly can print the news.

120
00:04:48,380 --> 00:04:51,380
And you are now making news.
